WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.088
When a domain is deployed, its name
becomes a DNS zone, its domain controllers

2
00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:10.525
become the authoritative servers, and
every domain-joined machine points at them.

3
00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:14.575
Nobody chose that as a DNS
architecture, but it is one.

4
00:00:14.575 --> 00:00:19.559
Storing zones in AD brings secure dynamic
updates and multi-master operation,

5
00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:22.013
and both disappear with the directory.

6
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:27.875
So the AD DNS estate breaks into seven
components, each needing its own decision:

7
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:30.984
integrated zones,
file-backed zones, stubs,

8
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:36.137
conditional forwarders, GlobalNames,
reverse zones and signed zones.

9
00:00:36.137 --> 00:00:40.917
One correction to the source: conditional
forwarders are easy to export,

10
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:43.625
because Windows stores each one as a zone.

11
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:45.400
The hard part isn't finding them.

12
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.686
It's deciding which of the forwarders
built up over the years for partners,

13
00:00:49.686 --> 00:00:52.130
trusts and retired systems still matter.
